title the reading that found its prose -- a notation's document is its comment block, and nineteen files said so with one number
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. The card named my next door outright: construction/standing-equipment.kyri reads C+ 75.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST, AND IT ANSWERED NONE. No reachable agents, so no peer was named before a file moved and nothing this lap touched is in flight elsewhere. The charter law from %291 is satisfied by asking rather than by the answer.
think ROTA ROW 2 -- FIRE, MARS, THE ROW THAT SEES. N is git rev-list --count HEAD = 3882, and 3882 mod 5 is 2; my last lap read row 0, so this is a step of two and row 1 goes unread between us. I am naming the skip rather than papering it, which is what the seed's own passage asks. Fire's question is what must stop and what must be cut, and its instruction is to look straight at the uncomfortable point rather than glance and guess. The lap that squints cuts twice. That is exactly what happened here: the comfortable move was to type --setting meter, watch C+ 75 become 100, and call the door closed.
think THE COLD OPEN WAS CLEAN AND I HELD STILL FOR IT. 109 guards, 106 green, 3 red, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close, tree_moved=no over a 25-minute pass. All three reds are the gates the card already names -- rule_twin at %7, pond_enclosure_door at %5, commit_message_guard at %393's untracked publisher -- so nothing new was wrong and my lane was clear. I read and measured while it ran and wrote no byte until it closed, since the runner digests the tree at both ends and an edit mid-pass kills the shell (%221).
think THE DOOR THE CARD NAMED WAS THE INSTRUMENT, NOT THE PAGE. Graded at all three settings construction/standing-equipment.kyri answered 75, 75, 100. A composite that moves only when Meter switches the reading OFF is a composite measuring nothing, and the line beside it said which half had been read: reach=0 (grade 327 against 9) over 1 sentences. A Flesch-Kincaid grade of 327 is not a hard page; it is a page that was never found.
think LINE 69 OF prose_register_scan.sh IS THE WHOLE MECHANISM. Its measure() skips /^[ \t]*[-*>#]/ as bullets, headings and quotes. In Markdown that is correct -- a heading is a title, not a sentence. In Kyri and Bron the # is the COMMENT sigil, and a roster keeps its entire document behind it. So both readings, Register and Reach, threw away 498 comment lines carrying 7,271 words and read the 457 records instead, which carry no terminal punctuation and therefore fuse into ONE 915-word pseudo-sentence rather than meeting the reading's own under-four-words floor one at a time. The floor was already right; nothing separated the records so it never got to apply.
think NINETEEN FILES, ONE NUMBER, AND THE NUMBER IS AN ARITHMETIC SIGNATURE. Every tracked .bron or .kyri carrying 200 words or more of comment prose read EXACTLY one sentence and EXACTLY composite 75 -- template-manifest.bron at 1,786 words of that one sentence, waymark-registry.bron at 606, domain-registry.bron at 434, seven Caravan system descriptors among them. 75 is 300/4: Reach floored at zero with Register, Truth and Service all perfect. That is the same C+ 75 the shape museum wore in %358, which is how I knew before reading a line of code that this was the same fault in a third family.
think WHY IT ARRIVED THROUGH A DOOR TWO REPAIRS HAD BUILT. %276 taught the program extractor # and //; %358 taught it Glow's ::. Both landed inside the program branch, which is where an extractor lives, and both correctly left the prose branch alone. %392 then put .bron and .kyri on the prose side of the classifier so truth_source would read them as prose -- correct again, a notation does cite everywhere -- and the one line that settles truth_source settles prose_path beside it. Three correct edits and the third family walked in on the wrong side. A repair aimed at a comment mark lands where the extractor is, and the fault walks in through the branch that has none.
think THE FIX IS THE PARALLEL %392 ALREADY DREW, NOT A NEW RULE. A third artifact_kind: .bron and .kyri classify as notation and prepare their own body -- each comment line gives up its #[ ]? sigil, each record line closes with a period of its own. measure() stays exactly one reading, cited and never copied; I changed only which text is handed to it, which is precisely what the program branch already does. %199's one-roof law is kept rather than bent.
think I CHECKED WHAT THE CHANGE MUST NOT MOVE BEFORE I MOVED ANYTHING. truth_source is a separate case statement and stays untouched, so %398's prose skip and comment_citation_scan.sh read what they read. The Meter shortcut had tested artifact_kind = prose by name, which would have silently un-freed every session log at Meter, so it tests != program instead. README.md, tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh and glow/rune_shape.rye read byte-identical before and after -- I ran the elder and the new card over each and diffed the three lines that matter.
obs THE HONEST READING IS NOT THE FLATTERING ONE, AND THAT IS THE POINT. standing-equipment.kyri now reads A 91 at Field and 86 at Door, so the card's named door closes above B without a word of the file rewritten -- and the reading it finally gives is 38% negative over 278 sentences, which is over both the Door and Field ceilings. That is a real finding the elder number could never have produced: the roster's prose is refusal-led, and Gauge's own answer for refusal-led prose is Meter. Which setting a roster takes can now be argued from a measurement rather than asserted, and I left that question named on the card rather than answering it in the same lap that built the instrument to ask it.
obs THE NINETEEN DISCRIMINATE NOW, WHICH IS THE TEST THAT MATTERS. They read 87 to 99 where all nineteen read 75. A meter whose output is constant across nineteen different inputs is not a strict meter; it is a disconnected one, and the difference is invisible from the passing side.
obs SIX OF EIGHT NEW CASES BITE AGAINST THE ELDER CARD, WHICH IS WHAT TELLS A REPAIR FROM A REWORDING. The control builds a second card in the pen with the classifier carried back, and reads the same two plants through it: warm and cold rosters with identical records and opposite heads come back IDENTICAL there, and the elder reading answers one sentence. The two legs that do not bite are the ones proving the change does NOT move something -- Meter still free, long field values still read -- and those are preservation legs rather than refusals, so I counted them as what they are.
obs THE WITNESS WAS RECITING TWO DIFFERENT COUNTS OF ITSELF. Its header said seventy-two behaviors and its closing say line said seventy-nine, in one file. Neither matched the control, which emits 83 yes/no readings. Both now read the counted 83 with a clause saying it was counted rather than recited, which is %110's lesson applied to the instrument that teaches it. Small, and it is exactly the drift class this lap was already reading.
obs FOLD RODE AHEAD OF WRITING, AS THE PIN'S OWN LAW ASKS. REDS stood at 22,338 of 24,576 and my row is 3,900, so %398 and %399 -- both CLOSED, both this lane's own closures from the last lap -- folded to one shelf first, taking the pin to 14,423 before a byte of my row was written. %374 and %360 are OPEN and stayed on the pin by that same law. I wrote the shelf header myself because reds_fold.sh refuses to invent one, which is the right refusal.
obs AND THEN THE SEND COLLIDED TWICE, AND THE LAW DECIDED BOTH TIMES RATHER THAN I DID. xy moved between my hot pass and my push, and again after the first rebase. Dream landed Scribe's baton reader; a peer then landed the citation scan's extension list AND published %400 and %401 AND folded %398 and %399 onto a shelf of their own. So: my row booked %400 at 09:56:37 and theirs booked %400 at 09:59:07 -- mine is the earlier stamp by two and a half minutes and theirs is the one that reached the anointed spine, and a published number never moves. My row renumbered to %402, stamp untouched, and reds_spine_derive reads rebindings=0 squatters=0 next_free=401 -> ok. My whole fold was withdrawn rather than merged, because theirs is published and two shelves holding the same two rows is the duplication %230's law exists to prevent. I deleted my shelf file, took their recital line, and rebuilt my row on their ledger. This is the second lap running that the same law has decided a collision for me, and it decided correctly both times.
obs THE CARD IS THE HONEST FAILURE OF THIS ROUND, AGAIN, AND IT IS WORSE THAN LAST TIME. Upstream landed it at 24,555 of 24,576 -- 21 bytes free -- so every byte I added had to come out of the live front. I cut my own paragraph four times, from 1,100 bytes to 500, released two clauses whose matters are CLOSED and shelved, and compressed the roster line to one fleet reading. It closes at 24,563: THIRTEEN bytes free. I criticized handing on a full pin last lap and I am handing on a fuller one. The structural question is unchanged and above this seat -- whether a pin two hands write inside one hour should carry both the standing directives and the live front under one bound -- and no amount of careful trimming answers it.
obs THE CARD IS AT 24,465 OF 24,576 AND THAT IS STILL THE STANDING PROBLEM. I cut the departing round's %398/%399 paragraph, compressed the roster readings to this pass, and trimmed my own front twice to fit the prior-lap row -- 111 bytes free. The fourth settled-decisions shelf that my last lap named as the fix has landed, so I removed that stale sentence; the structural question it was pointing at is unchanged and stays above this seat.
obs NO MOLT FRAME WAS OWED. Seven artifacts touched, every one B or better measured at molt time rather than at push time: the card 90, its control 95, its witness 88, standing-equipment.kyri 86 at Door, REDS 100, ITINERARY 95, the new shelf 100.
loom witness=qa_report_card wall_s=9 behaviors=83 notation_legs=8 elder_biting=6
loom witness=comment_citation wall_s=50 behaviors=17
loom roster=cold guards=109 green=106 red=3 tree_moved=no
file tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh the third artifact_kind -- notation prepares its own body, sigil off comments and a period on records
file tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card_control.sh eight cases, six of them read a second time through a card carrying the elder classifier
file tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish eight asserts, the notation paragraph, and both recited counts corrected to the counted 83
file construction/REDS.md books and closes %402 -- renumbered from %400 on the rebase, stamp untouched; headline derived to 402 rows
file construction/ITINERARY.md live front carries %402, merged onto upstream's own block; the stale fourth-shelf sentence removed
recommend check-in either -- **%402 is CLOSED on a witness that runs on metal in 9 seconds**, and the door the card named for this seat closes with it: `standing-equipment.kyri` was never below B, the instrument was reading its records instead of its document. The roster's three reds are unchanged and are the gates you already hold -- `rule_twin` %7, `pond_enclosure_door` %5, `commit_message_guard` at %393's untracked publisher. **One door is newly yours and it is a real question rather than a chore:** the corrected reading says `standing-equipment.kyri` is **38% negative over 278 sentences**, which is refusal-led prose whose Gauge answer is Meter -- so *which setting a roster takes* can now be settled by measurement, and nineteen notation files are waiting on that answer. **Two doors are where they were:** Door's ceiling of 9 against module heads that run 12-17, which is what puts 61 of 134 sampled sources below B; and gate %7, where `quality-assurance` is the rule roster's one `additive:claude` pair and carrying its three lines deletes nothing. **The card closes at 13 bytes free**, which is the round's honest failure: upstream landed it at 21 free, I cut my own paragraph to a fifth of its draft and released two closed-and-shelved clauses to fit, and the next hand still has nothing. **And one habit is worth carrying:** when a grade refuses to move, read what the instrument measured before reading what the page said -- three families have now worn the same C+ 75, and each time the number was the instrument's rather than the page's.
